Let me read the cluster-merge logic where the dir slot is "restored":
I've reached the relay boundary and found the **decisive root** of the residual resurrection. Let me record it precisely for continuation.

The resurrection is in `mxfs_iflush_cluster_merge_dirs` (xfs_inode.c:5508): it `memcpy(dbuf, ddisk, inodesize)` — overlays the **stale disk** image onto a dir slot whenever the buffer is *not strictly ahead* of disk. The guard at 5487-5506 only protects **adds** (`bsf->count > dsf->count`), not **removals** (buffer behind disk = our committed removal). So node2's `mv` removal (in_ail, not yet durable; disk still has `n2_i2_r1`) gets reverted by the overlay → resurrection. The `P119-NONEX in_ail=1` proves node2 had the committed change.
## Session 56 summary — major progress, criterion NOT yet met

**Criterion** (reliable 2-node dlm=tcp 17/17): **NOT met.** Improved from ~50% baseline to ~67% (s5✓ s6✗ s7✓), with two load-bearing fixes landed and the residual root now precisely identified.

### Two fixes landed (KEEP — verified load-bearing)
1. **Release-drain wait-until-clean** (`mxfs_inode_cluster_durable`, xfs_mxfs_dlm.c ~1684): on a BAST release (state DEMOTING/BAST), wait up to ~3s for the inode to leave the AIL instead of giving up after 50ms. **Eliminated the d11 drain-give-up interlock** (P9-ICD-FAIL → 0); suite went 50%→16/17.
2. **Partial-write skips any not-logged DIR slot** (`mxfs_submit_partial_inode_write`, xfs_buf.c ~1727): a dir's on-disk slot is written ONLY by its EX-holder's logged flush; every co-resident cluster flush leaves it untouched. Closed the co-resident stale-buffer resurrection path → s5/s7 PASS.

### Residual root — PROVEN this session (the remaining ~1/3 failures)
The durable dirent resurrection is `mxfs_iflush_cluster_merge_dirs` (xfs_inode.c **5508**): it overlays the **stale disk** image onto a dir slot that's *behind* disk. The count-guard (5487) only protects committed **adds** (buffer ahead), not committed **removals** (buffer behind). So a node's `mv`-removal that's in_ail-but-not-yet-durable gets reverted by the overlay → the removed dirent resurrects. Captured the full chain: `CONVBLK-DENY → self-demote → P51-REL drain_ms=0 → P119-NONEX in_ail=1 → P-CLMERGE restored`.

**Next-session fix (documented in ccmemory `sess56-ROOT2-clmerge-overlay-reverts-committed-removal`):** skip the overlay when the slot's in-core inode is `in_ail`/pinned (authoritative local delta) — same clean-gate principle as the reload-merge and the partial-write skip.

### Key accelerator discovered
`tests/tcp/repro_rename_drain.sh 150 N` reproduces the leak **standalone in ~2 min** (vs ~9 min full suite) — `mv` succeeds silently while the source dirent resurrects. (A separate sess13 AG-DLM deadlock shutdown appears only under heavy repro churn, ~iter 3-7; the full suite doesn't trigger it.)

Build in tree carries both fixes plus diagnostic probes; the dead `dirty==0` FUA-refresh was reverted (it caused a CORRUPT_INCORE shutdown — never FUA-read into a buffer mid-submit). The criteria marker is **not** written.

